# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your own values.
# `.env.local` is gitignored. Never commit a real key.

# Where the FastAPI backend is reachable FROM THE BROWSER.
# Local dev / docker compose on your own machine: leave as-is.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://localhost:8000

# ── TomTom Traffic (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers the live congestion overlay on the Surveillance map. Get a free key at
# https://developer.tomtom.com (Traffic Flow tiles; free tier is 2,500
# requests/day, which is ample for a demo).
#
# Leave this EMPTY and everything still works — the traffic toggle reports
# "no key configured" and the map falls back to the congestion overlay built
# from this platform's own vehicle_events. The app never hard-depends on it.
#
# SECURITY NOTE, because this is unavoidable rather than an oversight: anything
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the JavaScript the browser downloads,
# so this key IS visible to anyone who opens devtools. That is inherent to
# fetching map tiles directly from the browser. Mitigate it the way TomTom
# intends: in the TomTom dashboard, restrict the key to your own origins
# (http://localhost:3000 for local use) and keep it on the free tier. Do not
# reuse a key that has paid services attached to it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TOMTOM_API_KEY=
